    {
      "assumption": "Revenue recovers ~10% annually driven by fees, Stock Holding subsidiaries, and treasury income despite continued core loan book contraction and zero fresh loan sanctions.",
      "failure_scenario": "Stock Holding Corporation of India faces competitive pressure from discount brokers and declining retail participation in physical demat/depository services, compressing subsidiary fee income; simultaneously, rising interest rates erode mark-to-market treasury gains, resulting in revenue stagnation or further decline rather than the assumed 10% annual recovery.",
      "risk": "High"
